_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le12ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What Are Idioms?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Idioms are expressions which have a meaning apart from what the words themselves mean."}, {"type": "text", "content": "They are very common in spoken English. It is important to know some idioms and to remember that the meaning of the words as a group is different from the words individually. Here are some idioms:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Idiom \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He was drinking like a fish.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He was drinking a lot of alcohol.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Actions speak louder than words. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can judge people better based on what they do rather than what they say.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The ball is in your court. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The next decision is yours.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Don't judge a book by its cover. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Don't judge someone based only on their appearance.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Hit the nail on the head. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do or say something exactly right.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "More About The Past Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are some general rules to remember when you use the Past Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The word <span class=\"strong\">while </span> usually comes before the Past Continuous clause.  The word  <span class=\"strong\">when</span> usually comes before the Past tense.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">While we were ordering</span>, she kept giving him flirty looks. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">When the bill came</span>, he was looking at me like I had to pay for it. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to run into"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to meet someone unexpectedly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: We ran into his ex-girlfriend."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to describe someone."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cheapskate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who does not like to spend money"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: He is such a cheapskate!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flirty "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "acting like you are attracted to someone "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She was being very flirty with him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "speechless "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unable to speak because of shock or surprise "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)